{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual marginalized mixture likelihood implemented with `target += log_sum_exp(...)` and `bernoulli_lpmf(...)` by the algebraically equivalent built-in sampling statement `y ~ bernoulli(mixture_prob)`, where `mixture_prob = dot_product(cluster_weight, cluster_prob)`. For binary observations, `sum_k w_k Bernoulli(y | p_k)` is exactly `Bernoulli(y | sum_k w_k p_k)`, so the posterior/log density is preserved while avoiding arbitrary target manipulation. The input data are unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"// ForestDB translation: CrossCat
data {
  int<lower=1> K;
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;
}
parameters {
  simplex[K] cluster_weight;
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[K] cluster_prob;
}
model {
  real mixture_prob;
  cluster_weight ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0 / K, K));
  cluster_prob ~ beta(1, 1);
  mixture_prob = dot_product(cluster_weight, cluster_prob);
  y ~ bernoulli(mixture_prob);
}
generated quantities {
  int<lower=1, upper=K> cluster = categorical_rng(cluster_weight);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":5,"N":5,"y":[0,0,0,0,1]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
